# The kitty keyboard protocol's flag 16, report associated text, which acts
# with flag 8. Under flags 25 (1, 8 and 16), Shift+A sends the text A, 65, in
# a third field, as the specification's own example shows. Ctrl+A makes the
# control character 0x01, which the text field never holds, so it sends no
# text field.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Report associated text; ADR-1005 D13 slice 3
# capability: key-kitty-associated-text
size 20 2
send "\e[>25u\e[?u"
check
reply "\e[?25u"
key A mods=shift
key a mods=ctrl char="\x01"
check
reply "\e[97;2;65u\e[97;5u"
